    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG O'Sullivan Hurley are delighted to welcome this four-bedroom detached home set on a large landscaped circa half acre private site within walking distance of all amenities and services of Clarecastle village. Ennis town centre and the M18 Limerick/ Shannon/Galway motorway are accessible within minutes' drive making this an ideal property to take full advantage of countryside living and space yet being within easy walking and driving access to all services and amenities. \n\nThe property comprises natural stone front boundary wall with tarmac driveway and landscaped gardens with lawn areas to the front, side and rear complete with mature hedging, plants and shrubbery. The added advantage of being south facing to the rear with a large paved outdoor dining space overlooking the private gardens and farmlands to the rear of the dwelling. There is a large block built detached garage completing the exterior. Internally the property comprises four bedrooms all complete with built in wardrobes, ensuite, main bathroom, large main living room and open plan kitchen and dining area with conservatory just off with a utility completing the accommodation. The property has been upgraded in the last number of years and is presented in excellent decorative order throughout. Viewings are highly recommended and strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agent. PSL 002295"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - \nTiled flooring, coved ceiling, hotpress storage closet and attic access.\n\nLiving Room - 5.9m x 4.8m\nSolid oak timber flooring, coved ceiling, feature bay front aspect window, marble surround fireplace with gas inset fire, wall lights and centre light feature with double doors to kitchen/dining.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 8.8m x 3m\nKitchen area tiled flooring, built in wall and base units, splashback tiling, breakfast bar counter, space and plumbing for dishwasher and fridge freezer, large Rangemaster oven with gas hob and overhead extractor fan, eye level wall unit with inset lighting.Dining area laminate timber flooring and double doors to conservatory or living room to front to open up the entire living and family areas of the property.\n\nConservatory - 3.9m x 3.6m\nTiled flooring, wraparound windows overlooking rear garden, vaulted timber clad ceiling with main light feature, wall lights and double glass inset doors to rear garden.\n\nUtility Room - \nBuilt in wall and base units, space and plumbing for washing machine and dryer and door leading to rear garden.\n\nBedroom One - 2.7m x 2.6m\nLaminate timber flooring, front aspect window and built in wardrobe units.\n\nBedroom Two - 2.7m x 2.7m\nLaminate timber flooring, front aspect window and built in wardrobe units.\n\nBedroom Three - 4m x 2.7m\nLaminate timber flooring, front aspect window and built in wardrobe units.\n\nBedroom Four - 4.5m x 3m\nLaminate timber flooring, wall to wall built in wardrobes, coved ceiling, rear aspect window and connecting door to ensuite.\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - \nFully tiled, WC, wash hand basin with overhead mirror and shaver light, shower unit and side aspect window.\n\nBathroom - 3m x 1.8m\nFully tiled, WC, wash hand basin with overhead mirror and shaver light, shower unit, separate bath and rear aspect window.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Eircode V95R2P0</li><li> Total Floor Space approx. 133 m2 (1,432sq.ft.)</li><li> Built 1996</li><li> Mains Water</li><li> Private Sewage Treatment System</li><li> Mains Gas Central Heating</li><li> Fibre Broadband</li><li> Upgraded Walls and Attic Insulation</li><li> 0.47 acres Site</li><li> Fully Alarmed</li><li> Fibre Broadband</li><li> South Facing Rear Garden</ul>"
